\pard\plain\f1\fs28\b Sample RTF Document\b0\fs22\par
\pard\plain\f0\fs22\par
This document demonstrates that AILANG Parse extracts text from Rich Text Format files\par
deterministically, including international characters and CP1252 escapes.\par
\par
\b Internationalisation\b0\par
\par
Danish words: K\u248?bsaftale, \u248?konomi, sm\u248?rrebr\u248?d, fj\u230?rkr\u230?, \u229?l.\par
French phrases: caf\u233? au lait, premi\u232?re classe, na\u239?vet\u233?.\par
German nouns: Stra\u223?e, Br\u252?cke, \u196?pfel, Gr\u246?\u223?e.\par
Greek alphabet sample: \u945?, \u946?, \u947?, \u948?, \u949?.\par
\par
\b CP1252 hex escapes\b0\par
\par
Currency: 50\'a3 pounds sterling, 100\'80 euro, 250\'a5 yen, copyright \'a9 1999.\par
Smart quotes: \'93like these\'94 and \'91these\'92.\par
Punctuation: em dash \'97 en dash \'96 bullet \'95 ellipsis \'85 trademark \'99.\par
\par
\b Tab-separated form fields\b0\par
\par
Name:\tab Jane Doe\par
Email:\tab jane@example.com\par
Phone:\tab +44 20 7946 0958\par
Reference:\tab AIL-2026-0518\par
\par
\b Numbered observations\b0\par
\par
1. Parser is pure AILANG with no external dependencies.\par
2. CP1252 hex escapes (\\'XX) decode via a built-in Windows-1252 table.\par
3. Unicode escapes (\\uNNNN?) reassemble as UTF-8 using std/bytes.\par
4. Header destinations like \\fonttbl and \\stylesheet are skipped entirely.\par
5. Starred destinations ({\\*\\generator ...}) are skipped including nested groups.\par
\par
\b Closing notes\b0\par
\par
RTF was originally specified by Microsoft in 1987 and remains a common interchange\par
format for legal, government, and template-heavy workflows. Even modern Word still\par
writes RTF on demand, which is why parsing it without a heavyweight dependency is\par
useful for batch document pipelines.\par
